1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gero was balabat of Mecha. He initially refused to submit to Ras Gobena, when he came to incorporate the region into (the future) Menelik II's rule. Thanks to skillful mediation by an intermediary Blatta who presen
2 CONC ted it as a mutually respectful arrangement, he agreed and exchanged gifts of clothes for cattle, and got recognition from Menelik of his rule over his father Godana's territory. He sent his first son Reba to serve under Gobena, b
2 CONC ut after Reba got into trouble, the next son Wami was sent to serve under Gobena.   (Source: Yebegaw Mebreq, biography of Jagema Kelo.). 
2 CONT
2 CONT This occurred before the battle of Embabo, which was  in 1882. Since Gero had grown sons, this means Gero was probably born well before 1840.
