1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.friesian.com/ethiopia.htm Rema Armah of Abyssinia (760-825) was the king of Abyssinia from 775 to 825, succeeding Ayzur of Abyssinia and preceding Degna Djan of Abyssinia. Rema Armah was born to King Ayz
2 CONC ur of Abyssinia, a monarch of the Miaphysite Christian Solomonic dynasty of Abyssinia. Rema Armah succeeded his father upon his death in 775 and was king for fifty years. When he died in 825, he was succeeded by his son Degna Djan
